# .env.example
#
# A blank form for the settings each app needs to talk to the backend.
#
# HOW TO USE: copy this file to a new file named ".env" INSIDE the app's own
# folder (apps/home/.env or apps/staff/.env) and fill in the values. Ask Shafin
# for the real values. The ".env" file is private and is never shared in git.
#
# The anon key below is NOT a secret password: it is the "public" key that every
# phone with the app carries. The database's security rules are what protect
# the data. NEVER put the "service role" key in any app. That one is secret.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
